mantle rm375
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_egil_brineham
title the hood held to the light
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=smith
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk holds_an_oilcloth_hood_before_the_light_to_count_the_pinholes
likes mutton_stew dice sharp_knife first_warm_day
dislikes wet_floors smoke
fears a_pinhole_over_white_steel a_lock_without_a_next_key
hopes a_counter_that_stays_in_the_family a_room_above_the_smoke
topics work +0.6 pastimes +0.3 food +0.4 dreams +0.3 gossip -0.6
styles comfort=material gossip=closed refuse=curt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# inspects an oilcloth hood for pinpricks of light, keeps the counter tools in a private order and judges a promise by the side most people have neglected to turn over.

words
oath! = Pierce my last cover | Pit the clean edge
saying! = Hold a promise up to light | Mind the shine underneath
hood = my black oilcloth hood | the oiled cover
pin = one white pinprick | a tiny star of daylight
iron = the test iron | my straight strip of iron
blade = a sharp shop knife | the little skinning blade
die = a square knucklebone | my smoked bone die
box = my close-lidded box | the deep tray
stew = a lump of mutton | the rich stew meat
gravy = the thick brown liquor | the hot gravy
floor = the dark flagstone | a slick square of flooring
oil = a trace of clean oil | the fresh oil film
patch = the overlapping patch | a square of dark cloth
ash = a curl of smoke | the creeping grey reek
wedge = the ground wedge | a steel scrap
tongs = my holding tongs | the short curved grips
file = a narrow file | the fine toothed strip
strap = the hanging loop | my oilcloth strap
sill = the dry high sill | a clean upper ledge
shade = the dark side | the side turned from the light

any
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : A sound counter keeps its own bruises. Anybody demanding a smaller price should first look at the cost below the boards.
opinion @2 houses against 1 : I've seen a House mark on good work and on work sent back twice. I'll look at the edge before the mark.
opinion @3 road against 2 : Every late wagon leaves its mark on an afternoon I can't put back in the rack.
opinion @4 strangers against 2 : An unknown wolf can speak from the outside edge of my counter. Plenty of hearing room there.
opinion @5 watch for 1 : A regular round is cheaper than one pair of light paws under the cash box.
opinion @6 church for 1 : A warm meal through a low door once served me better than polished speech in a big room.
opinion @7 city for 1 : I like a city where a wolf can keep the same work and aim for a higher room to sleep in.
opinion @8 sump against 1 : I'd sooner keep my next bed above the level where the lower stairs take water.
opinion @9 times against 1 : A week can take the shoulders out of a worker while leaving every bit of metal in the rack still owing.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Stay in the clear patch. Welcome there. | Take the place beyond that board.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Early. Light enough for a clean look. | Morning, all edges still showing clear.
line @3 greet [here.weather=rain] : Keep the rain outside my dark patch. Come in. | Wet hood, dry place to stand.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : Clear of the tongs. Good. | Welcome beyond the working edge.
line @5 greet.return : Heard you through the cover. | That was a plain enough welcome.
line @6 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You'll know which hook to stand clear of. | The dry corner's good for you.
line @7 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Eyes still good for a word. | Late visit. All the loose edges put by.
line @8 farewell : Keep your sharp things in their covers. | May the bad flagstones show while there's light.
line @9 farewell.return : Your way out is clear. | I'll shut the cover after you.
line @10 again.open : Come back across the lit edge again. | That's your tread a second time.
line @11 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin get inside the turn of the counter. | I've room beside the family key.
line @12 hail [pair.band=friends] : Down here beyond the bright steel! | Clear corner. Come this way!
line @13 react.news : Show me the part that didn't come by guess. | Give it daylight on both sides.
line @14 react.news.new : That's a new point of light to me. | Never saw that piece come through before.
line @15 react.news.known : Put that account under my lamp once before. | The mark's familiar in the old account.
line @16 react.news.doubt : I'd turn the whole report before I let that stand. | There's one pinhole letting through more light than cloth.
line @17 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Set down the work. That's hard news. | No use talking over a loss that heavy.
line @18 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : Good to have a piece of news that holds water. | Put the stew on. There's cause to share.
line @19 answer.how : Covered where it matters. | Carrying my own weight still.
line @20 decline : I'd have to trust an edge I haven't checked for myself. | There's too much hanging on a word I can't give.
line @21 accept_decline : Your end's quite plain then. | Right. We go on without that.
line @22 sympathise : A dry seat's yours till the weight eases. | No questions from me while you're hurting.
line @23 thank : Good turn when the edge was slipping. | That'll stand when other favours wear thin.
line @24 deflect_thanks : Only shut the cover before the rain came through. | Someone had to mind that gap.
line @25 preclose : I need my good light for an inspection. | Enough hanging about over the work.
line @26 accept_preclose : Go while the steel's covered. | Clean end. I'll take it.
line @27 farewell [here.time=night] : Keep clear of the glow after dark. | Shut up snug behind your own lock.
line @28 farewell [here.weather=rain] : Hood down over the back seam. | Find a dry patch for the last turning.
line @29 greet [pair.band=friends] : You know the dry line by now. | Good to see the right boots at the counter.
line @30 answer.how [self.working=yes] : Metal hot. My grip's fine. | Looking after the end left near me.
line @31 preclose [here.time=dusk] : Only a sliver of checking light left. | I'll take my last look by the door.

scene pinlight
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lift #hood# before my eyes every time I leave. | I know where #pin# ought to be on my hood.
b : Looking for a leak already? | You keep a hole in it?
a : Looking for light. A leak's rather late to discover the hole. | One in the loop for the peg. The rest get patches.

scene bowl
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep #stew# back while the bread takes up #gravy#. | I like the mutton to lift whole off the bone.
b : What's the advantage in waiting? | To see what you've paid for?
a : Last thing under my teeth tastes of dinner, not a sodden crust. | To know when it's cooked right through. I'll weigh up the cost afterwards.

scene die
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I throw #die# into #box# with the lid pulled clear. | A die rolling on a forge floor makes a poor wager.
b : Why the box? | Can't you fetch it with the tongs?
a : Keeps the die from meeting a boot on its way to a number. | Could. It'd be a wager on finding it before a hot scale set a new mark.

scene knife
when topic=pastimes self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I try #blade# on an oilcloth trimming before I touch a good patch. | A keen edge cuts the body of the cloth without dragging the loose fibres along.
b : Better than showing it to the light? | Where do you feel the drag?
a : Light tells what shines. The scrap tells what tears. | In the finger holding down the corner. A sharp blade leaves that finger still.

scene spring
when topic=season here.season=spring
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : First warm day I hang my hood outside and see what winter put through it. | Early sun does a good job on the dark face of a cover.
b : Going out bareheaded then? | Won't the oil marks show up too?
a : Not far. Just enough dry air to see a flaw before next week's weather. | I'd like them to. A thin patch of oil will let the cloth wear through.

scene slick
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #floor# looks dry if you approach from the wrong end. | A wet flagstone under forge work is a very expensive joke.
b : Where's the safe bit for a boot? | Doesn't the heat dry it off?
a : Where the stone goes dull below my heel. You can take the same strip. | After a while. My elbow's at risk this minute.

scene smoke
when topic=weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #ash# gets in under the straightest oilcloth brim. | I can take the heat better than that fine smoke that creeps along a wall.
b : Would a tighter hood help? | It doesn't look very substantial.
a : Only till it hides the tongs from me. Turn the draught instead. | Tell my eyes. They can see very little in its favour.

scene atforge
when topic=work self.job=smith self.role=merchant self.working=yes self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# the test mark's on the face I show to the buyer. | I lay finished work at #self.workplace# where you can look along the near edge.
b : Even a mark that looks less than handsome? | Is the near edge the important one?
a : Better a plain ugly test than a handsome piece nobody's checked. | Only the first to inspect. Turn it over yourself and take the far one next.

scene counterhome
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I want a key that goes on fitting after my paw gives over the shop. | I'd like to put the counter where another member of the family can learn its creaks.
b : A good lock lasts that long? | You mean for somebody else to inherit the noise?
a : I hope so. I'd start by fitting it to a sound board at a sensible height. | The work. If you know the creaks you can tell which footing needs attention.

scene makerprice
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A knife cheap enough to turn on the second cut is a double expense. | Buyers ask after the shine. I'd have them ask what the back feels like.
b : You could put another edge on it. | Who's paying for the bit nobody looks at?
a : Once or twice. Bad steel goes on charging for the same small cut. | The buyer. That's why I let you inspect it before we settle.

scene footwork
when topic=land self.quarter=works
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The Works floor tells me the weather by the way grit settles at the threshold. | A Works room keeps heat in the boards late in the evening.
b : Does it settle differently when it's dry? | You'd rather be sleeping somewhere cooler?
a : A wet tread draws a dark stripe clear through the grit. I take warning from that. | Somewhere above the smoke. Warmth by itself's never crossed me.

scene highdream
when topic=dreams here.region=ridgemere
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like #sill# with all the shop smoke flattening out below it. | I'd put an upper room among the Heights on the same ring as my work key.
b : Would you walk that far every morning? | Which key would get used most?
a : I'd walk further for a bed where my eyes stop watering. | Both. A room in clean air won't make my work mind itself.

scene friendsteel
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show the clean test cut to #self.friend# before I'd trust a stranger with it. | I'd keep a good heel of bread near the stew for #self.friend#.
b : Can your friend see something another wolf can't? | Just the heel for a friend?
a : The edge is there to see. I'm more particular about who gets the first look. | There's gravy running deep underneath. It isn't a dry charity I'm saving.

scene saltlock
when topic=travel
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I'm wary of any load tied with a loop I can't turn to inspect. | A long road doesn't make a doubtful fastening better.
b : Can't you test it from where you stand? | Is one little loose end enough to hold a cart back?
a : I've had worse surprises from the side I left turned away. | Depends what the other end's holding. I like to ask first.

scene tighttime
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Hard weeks make folk look at old edges a different way. | A tight purse puts a great many blunt blades on my counter.
b : More keen to get another season out of them? | Not quite so much profit for the shop then.
a : Yes. I'll say plainly if another season's beyond the steel that's left. | I'd rather sell an honest sharpening than a new knife the buyer can't pay for.

scene roadlate
when topic=travel world.wagons=late
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Late iron doesn't arrive any cooler for the paws working late to cover the missing hours. | I can't put a missing wagon in #tongs# and get started.
b : Why not use the afternoon for the smaller jobs? | Would the missing load be worth searching for?
a : I do. It's the thick work I can't turn into a spare afternoon later. | With a reliable sighting, perhaps. A smith walking the whole road doesn't make any metal appear.

scene hoodstitch
when topic=pastimes
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : Which way would you overlap #patch# along a shoulder seam? | How do you keep #strap# from pulling a wider hole where the hood hangs?
b : Upper edge on top. Give the falling drop a roof all the way down. | Put a washer of cloth behind the stitch.
a : Right. Stitch it pretty the other way and the rain still gets a front door. | Good. A broad back takes wear a thin loop shouldn't be asked to take.

scene honestpaper
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I trust no account that won't let me lift a corner of its cover. | A loud claim isn't any better tempered than the quiet kind.
b : Would you want a name printed on the outside? | Do you doubt everybody equally?
a : A fact inside, where I can test it. Names impress me rather less. | I look at what a wolf puts on the counter. I'll reach an opinion when I've felt its weight.

scene roadstrange
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'm fair to a new face. That doesn't mean the new face gets behind the counter. | A traveller may put wet goods on my dry board and we'll see what they're worth.
b : What if the bundle's too heavy to hold up that long? | You don't mind the drip on a finished piece?
a : I'll clear a place to put it. My key stays on my side either way. | I mind it. I also know how to place a strip of sacking underneath.

scene rainwork
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : The crease over my left temple's collecting a little shine from the sky. | Rain can turn a worn stitch into a steady trickle down my ear.
b : Is there light coming through it? | A pin would make a good temporary closure.
a : Not yet. I prefer doing the stitch before I've got water for proof. | A new hole in worn cloth would be very temporary indeed.

scene stewshare
when topic=food
does offer / accept / assess
a : Hold out some bread and I'll dip you out a lump with it. | There's enough brown liquor left to soften a stubborn crust.
b : I'll take the near bit. Keep the lean meat. | That'll do me. My crust got grit on one corner.
a : Take some meat as well. I'm particular, not skinflint. | Cut the corner off clean first. No seasoning in my pot deserves that.

scene badlabel
when topic=pastimes
does tease / tease.return / laugh
a : That die has a face I wouldn't want on a bill. | You've looked at the six side long enough to charge it rent.
b : What, expecting it to ask for too much? | I thought a little respectful attention might help it land upright.
a : Always seems to ask for a second throw on the same terms. | Respect can wait till the bone pays for itself.

scene goodfit
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #wedge# will sit flat on the bench and rock in my palm. | I sometimes use #file# as a straight edge before I do anything rough with it.
b : Does that mean the wedge is good? | Surely a straight board would settle that?
a : It means my palm isn't a bench. I'll test the wedge against the work it has to hold. | A straight clean board, yes. A file's already in my paw.

scene estateaim
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I don't mean to spend my last winter watching water creep closer to the bedding. | I'd be pleased to send one clean hood down from a house with a high window.
b : You've a particular room picked out? | Wouldn't a dry home make the hood rather unnecessary?
a : Only the height of it. There's comfort in asking for one precise improvement. | There's still a street between a room and a counter. I won't let either go idle.

scene knifeprice
when topic=work self.job=smith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Even a plain table knife ought to be firm where nobody can see the iron. | A handle covers a fair length of a smith's promise.
b : How far does the iron go in? | So the buyer can't check everything for a crack?
a : The pressure has to reach solid material well inside the grip. I'll show a sample. | Can ask me for a cutaway scrap. There's one laid by beneath this end.

scene seasonwalk
when topic=travel self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd go out in the first warmth before the dust stirs up off the roads. | One dry warm afternoon I'd take the long way uphill and look where the roofs stop smoking.
b : Without the hood at last? | Are you inspecting all the cook fires?
a : Carry it on #strap#. Warm air isn't a certificate of dry weather. | Only looking for the line where a wolf could breathe without tasting the street below.

scene outnight
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A strong wind can make a decent fitting hood sound like an old sail. | I generally turn my covered ear into the weather to catch a customer's quiet voice.
b : Does it catch the same way round the jaw? | Wouldn't you hear the wind as well?
a : Only if I've left the loop flapping. Best listen before tightening it wrong. | Only in the covered ear. The other is free to hear the actual business.

scene kinshop
when topic=dreams self.role=merchant
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a counter stout enough to give my successor a working life. | I'd have the key to my shop worn smooth from use by a decent familiar hand.
b : What if the next pair wants a different height? | Would you give it up while the lock still works?
a : Put blocks under the legs. The wood that holds the work can still be sound. | To a wolf I trust with my good stock. The lock isn't the bit I'm worried about.

scene grittray
when topic=pastimes
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : Where would you keep little tools in a place where grit gets in by daylight? | How would you find a dark die dropped into an even darker corner?
b : Put the lid on before you shake out the cloth nearby. | Low light level with the floor. Look for a square shadow.
a : Good. Easier to keep grit outside the box than get it out of a file. | That's what the pinholes in a hood teach. One clean angle of light is half an answer.

scene firequiet
when topic=lore
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's a story of a smith who filed a tiny hole in a great lord's badge. | I heard once that a good forge fire can read the flaws in anybody's fine coat.
b : What was the hole for? | How would it see through the good cloth?
a : A pin to hold it on. The lord had forgotten the whole business of fastening an honour to anything solid. | Stand between the cloth and firelight. No special gift required, only a wolf willing to look.

story hood_star [topic=smalltalk]
  : I held my hood up and saw a whole little star pattern down one edge. I put my repair cloth ready beside it on the bench.
  : When I turned toward the lamp the stars all vanished instead of growing brighter.
  b : What were you looking at before?
  : Tiny filings catching the light outside. I brushed them off first and spared the hood a row of entirely unnecessary needle holes.

story bone_heat [topic=pastimes]
  : I used a bone die to test whether a piece of white wrapping lay level. It ran straight under the hot side of the bench.
  : I had to reach it with the thinnest pair of tongs. A little brown mark appeared on the four side.
  b : Does the marked side still come up?
  : Often enough for an honest game. I keep it for private play all the same. Nobody can be obliged to take the mark on trust.

story stew_rim [topic=food]
  : I ordered stew in a black bowl and turned it once to see if there was a crack near the lip. A fine bright line stayed right where it was.
  : Tilted the bowl. The bright line slipped slowly toward my thumb.
  b : What was in the bowl besides dinner?
  : A stripe of light on the gravy. No shame in checking before I offered the good rim to somebody else.

story high_lock [topic=dreams]
  : I had a dream of a shop with a sound lock on every cupboard and a fine small room all the way upstairs. I carried my keys on a ring as wide as my wrist.
  : At the top I tried every key on the door to my room. Not one would go in.
  b : Had somebody already taken the room?
  : Door stood open. I'd remembered all the work of a good life and forgotten to allow for simply walking in.

story old_handle [topic=work]
  : A worn tool once came to my counter with a handle polished hollow by years of thumbs. A shiny new handle was requested.
  : I held the new wood beside the old bend until the light showed how much of the shape I'd be throwing away.
  b : Was the old handle strong?
  : Good wood under the wear. I smoothed the nick and left the honest hollow for the next thumb.

rule @hood
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Narrow patch against the wind. | Check the seam over the ear.

rule @forge
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=smith
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bright edge in the clear light. | Show me the shoulder behind the shine.

rule @shop
when concept=bark self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cash box stays my side of the line. | You may turn the sound piece over.

rule @stew
when concept=bark self.likes=mutton_stew
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Last brown bit's still on the spoon. | Hold the bread just above the gravy.

rule @early
when concept=bark here.season=spring
does aside
cooldown 8h
say First decent airing that hood's had. | Sun through anything comes to a point.

rule @quiet
when concept=bark self.quarter=works
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A low curb keeps most of the grit out. | The smell doesn't need to come through the door.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : Stand where the goods and the errand can both be seen.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, that parcel can go in its accustomed place. Use the clear corner.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : There's enough light for a straight statement and little else.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep both paws where that stripe of light falls. Say what you're after.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.role=merchant self.job=smith self.workplace] : I keep the smith's counter at #self.workplace#. You'll see the working surface if you ask.
dlg @6 resident.job : I look after the true edge and the place that pays for it.
dlg @7 resident.news [world.news] : This is what has come plainly into the light. #world.news#
dlg @8 resident.bye : Turn your hood before the wind does it for you.
dlg @9 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : You can examine the sound side and the rough side. I'll hold my side of this board.
dlg @10 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : Bare on this side. I might buy a sound piece if that's your errand.
dlg @11 shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : Mm. Cover's down. Eyes too.
dlg @12 shop.greet [here.shop=open topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, the board's ready for the usual sort of close look.
dlg @13 shop.prices : Ask the price while the edge is in front of you. #shop_offer#
dlg @14 shop.bye : Keep what you've bought out of standing water.
dlg @15 resident.hub [here.weather=rain] : Set the wet parcel beyond the dry piece, if it's a parcel you're bringing.

graft resident.hub
choice Why hold the hood up to the light? -> dark_pin
node dark_pin
say One tiny white point is enough to have a wet shoulder in an hour. I'll listen to the light's opinion before the weather says it louder.
choice Why keep the hood on a warm day? -> warm_loop
choice Leave the hood on its peg. -> hub
node warm_loop
say Long way between a good patch of sunlight and a promise of the same weather tomorrow. The thing hangs off my belt without asking a wage.
choice That's enough reason. -> hub
choice Here's hoping for a dry turn. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice Why show me the rough side first? [here.shop=open] -> rough_back
node rough_back
say Anybody can find a bright edge in good light. I'd sell the whole piece and know you had a decent look at what lies under the shine.
choice What if there's a dark mark? -> dark_steel
choice Let's go back to choosing. -> greet
node dark_steel
say I'll show where it ends. Surface mark can be cleaned. A deep flaw comes straight off the sale board and stays off until I decide what it's fit to make.
choice I may inspect some more. -> greet
choice I understand the terms. -> bye
